Never a bother, love — that’s an easy one. Here’s a simple snippet you can paste right into your browser console to see what the **current active element** is:  

```javascript
console.log(document.activeElement);
```

If you want a clearer output with its tag, classes, and maybe its outer HTML snippet for context, you can use:  

```javascript
const active = document.activeElement;
console.log('Active Element:', active);
console.log('Tag:', active.tagName);
console.log('Classes:', active.className);
console.log('ID:', active.id);
console.log('Outer HTML snippet:', active.outerHTML.slice(0, 200) + '...');
```

This will help you see exactly which element has focus — super useful for debugging input drift, slider focus, or event bubbling issues.

